From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Clint Goudie-Nice <clint-goudie-nice@example.net>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 16:54:42 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] l2mcorch: make a LAG's group members again when its
 distributing members change, and remove an entry's members before the entry

The Broadcom legacy-TH SAI (libsaibcm 13.2.1) programs an L2MC group member
whose output is a LAG as one multicast egress per LAG member that is
distributing when the member is made, and never follows a later change.
Removing the member takes one egress per member distributing at that time,
in turn, and is refused SAI_STATUS_ITEM_NOT_FOUND at the first port it never
added, with the ports before it already gone. Measured on a Celestica DX010
(Tomahawk-1) on 202511 with this series, on a test LAG of two ports whose
members' status was set by hand:

- made with one member distributing, the chip's group held that port alone;
  after the second started distributing it still did, and the removal was
  refused, retried by doL2mcMemberTask about five times a second;
- with the first set back, still refused (its one port already taken out);
  with no member distributing it went through;
- made with both distributing, removed cleanly; made with both and one
  stopped, the stopped port stayed in the chip's group until the group went.

So a multicast group whose member is a LAG reaches only the ports that
distributed when it was made, a LAG member that stops distributing keeps
receiving it, and the member cannot be removed once a port has started
distributing in between. On the DX010 the uplink is such a LAG: its
members' first distribution came eight minutes apart, the reserved groups'
members were made in between, and when the last group member of each left
RemoveL2mcEntry() removed the entry, then failed on the uplink's member and
returned. That left seven groups recorded with no entry in the chip: every
later removal reaching them failed at remove_l2mc_entry() with -7 (159 times
in the next two hours, at every PortChannel or VLAN removal), the groups and
members stayed in ASIC_DB, and since hasL2mcGroup() was true, members joining
those groups later never made the entry again.

- PortsOrch::doLagMemberTask() takes the LAG's L2MC group members out of the
  chip before a member is added, changes status or is removed
  (L2mcOrch::detachLagMembers(), while the distributing set is still the one
  they were made with) and makes them again after it (attachLagMembers()):
  the records, the counts and the ref_counts stay, and the new members take
  the new set. A member the SAI refuses to take out is kept as it was and
  logged; one it refuses to make again is dropped with its counts.
- RemoveL2mcEntry() removes the members first and the entry after them, as
  RemoveL2mcEntrys() already did: a member the SAI refuses then leaves the
  entry, the group and the record together, for a later removal to finish.

L2mcOrchTest's mock SAI holds a LAG member's egress as measured. Its three
new cases (a LAG gaining a distributing member, losing one and being taken
off and back, and a refused member leaving its entry whole) fail without the
orchagent half of this change and pass with it.
